    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0884" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–252: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-04T18:17:00-05:00">January 4,
                            1952—6:17 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gadel 594. Re Indians in South Africa.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>We approve additional para re neutral individual Delga 823 Jan 2.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We approve Del decision 21 Dec abstain on third preambular para and
                        operative paras 2 and 3 of draft Res (Delga 754 and 770 Dec 20).</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Del shld also abstain on the second preambular para in view of fact we
                        voted against para 3 of Res last year which South Africans are now charged
                        with contravening.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>In accordance position paper SD/A/C.1/360,
                        Del shld vote against para placing item on agenda seventh session.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>In vote on Res as whole Del authorized vote in favor as Res generally
                        similar to last year’s Res on which we voted affirmatively in plenary.
                            Dept convinced, however, Res unlikely
                        accomplish anything and there is risk that coming on top present SW African
                        situation it will make return S African Del to GA more difficult.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
